{"kind":"panel","id":"45cff134-9238-4128-8c62-96f5a0263e6b","type":"59e0b89a-e487-49f8-bab8-b5bab16be14c","name":"Panel","nick":"Column domain","desc":"A panel for custom notes and text values","box":[0,-360,560,300],"src":[],"text":"Column domain - the Alpaca4d Interaction Domain example.\n\nA 400 x 600 column of C30/37, 4 phi 25 at the corners and 2 phi 20 at mid-height, in design values: Concrete01 with fcu = fco is Eurocode 2's parabola-rectangle, Steel01 with b = 0 is elastic-perfectly plastic. Interaction Domain holds the concrete to 3.5 per mille (2 per mille at point C in full compression) and the bars to eud = 1 %.\n\nAxial resistance: -5117 kN in compression (fcd Ac + 400 MPa As), 1127 kN in tension.\n\nDomain Check, N held:\n  N -2000, My 250, Mz 80: SF 1.59\n  N -1000, My 400, Mz 150: SF 0.89 - it fails\n  N -3000, My 100, Mz 60: SF 2.74\nSwitch Method to Proportional: 1.42, 0.88, 1.44 - the third is axial-dominated, and N grows with the moments.\n\nIn Rhino: the section at the origin, then Domain 3D, the N-M diagram (turn Angle) and the My-Mz diagrams at the checks' N, with each check in black and where it meets the boundary in red.","colour":[0,0,0,0]}
